---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { AppearanceLab } from '../components/AppearanceLab';
import { appearanceSkinPolicy, appearanceSkinRecipes } from '../lib/appearance-skin-catalogue';
import { GitBranch } from '@lucide/astro';
const labels: Record<string, string> = {
  plate: 'Surface',
  edge: 'Panel edge',
  radius: 'Corner',
  field: 'Field',
  action: 'Action',
  focus: 'Focus',
  pressure: 'Measured weight',
};
---
<Base title="Appearance skins for App Composer" description="Try Composer’s two optional admin skins, compare them with the default, and read the finite contract an owner or agent implements. Sound and haptics stay off until you enable them.">
 <div class="appearance-intro">
  <h1>Two skins. One set of controls.</h1>
  <p class="lede">Composer’s administration can wear a tactile skin without changing a label, an action or a permission. Try both here, compare either with the default, and read the contract a fresh agent can implement.</p>
  <p class="small">This page is a public reference, not a second theme editor. The saved admin appearance lives in Brand Studio and needs the signed-in EmDash administrator.</p>
 </div>

 <AppearanceLab client:load />

 <section class="appearance-contract" aria-labelledby="contract-title">
  <h2 id="contract-title">The contract</h2>
  <p>A skin is a recipe with fixed choices. The compiler turns those choices into Composer tokens and edges; an owner’s text, a remote stylesheet, an image, a font, an animation or a new action can never enter it.</p>
  <div class="appearance-recipes">
   {appearanceSkinRecipes.map((recipe) => (
    <article>
     <h3>{recipe.name}</h3>
     <p>{recipe.description}.</p>
     <dl>
      {(['plate','edge','radius','field','action','focus','pressure'] as const).map((key) => (
       <div><dt>{labels[key]}</dt><dd>{recipe[key]}</dd></div>
      ))}
     </dl>
    </article>
   ))}
  </div>
  <h3>What every skin keeps</h3>
  <ul>
   {appearanceSkinPolicy.map((line) => <li>{line}</li>)}
   <li>16px fields, at least 44px actions and a visible keyboard focus ring in both native themes.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>How it is stored</h3>
  <p>The existing <code>composer.admin-brand/1</code> record carries <code>skin</code> and <code>skinPressure</code>. Records saved before skins existed normalise to <code>composer</code> and pressure 2, so retained versions still preview, restore and export. The default skin emits no CSS layer at all.</p>
  <h3>Adding a skin</h3>
  <ol>
   <li>Add one recipe in <code>src/lib/appearance-skin-catalogue.ts</code>. Every field is required and the id must be unique.</li>
   <li>Run <code>node scripts/appearance-skins.mjs --write</code> to regenerate the finite preview sheet.</li>
   <li>Run <code>node --test tests/appearance-skin.test.mjs</code> and <code>pnpm check</code> on the final tree.</li>
   <li>Inspect the skin at 390px and a laptop width, in light and dark, with keyboard only and reduced motion.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="small">A recipe that only looks different does not qualify. It has to keep every control usable, focused and readable.</p>
  <div class="appearance-links">
   <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/app-composer/blob/main/docs/brand-studio.md"><strong>Brand Studio documentation</strong><span>Save, preview, publish and restore the admin appearance.</span></a>
   <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/app-composer/blob/main/docs/appearance-skin-contract.md"><strong>The written contract</strong><span>Fields, compiler, sensory rules and the checks a fresh agent can run.</span></a>
   <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/app-composer/tree/main/src/lib/appearance-skin-catalogue.ts"><GitBranch size={16} aria-hidden="true"/><strong>Source</strong><span>The recipes and the compiler.</span></a>
  </div>
  <p class="small">Sound and haptics on this page use your browser’s Web Audio and vibration support. A browser that exposes neither still gets the visible pressed edge and every control. No physical phone was used to verify vibration strength.</p>
 </section>
</Base>
<style>
 .appearance-intro{max-width:900px}
 .appearance-intro h1{font-size:clamp(2.4rem,5vw,4.2rem);max-width:20ch;text-wrap:balance;margin:0 0 18px}
 .appearance-intro .lede{max-width:66ch;font-size:1.15rem}
 .appearance-intro .small{max-width:68ch}
 .appearance-contract{border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);margin-top:56px;padding-top:32px;max-width:1100px}
 .appearance-contract h2{font-size:2rem;margin:0 0 14px}
 .appearance-contract h3{font-size:1.3rem;margin:32px 0 10px}
 .appearance-contract p,.appearance-contract li{max-width:72ch}
 .appearance-contract ul,.appearance-contract ol{padding-left:22px;display:grid;gap:8px}
 .appearance-contract code{font-size:0.9em;background:var(--color-surface);padding:2px 5px;border-radius:4px}
 .appearance-recipes{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:24px;margin-top:20px}
 .appearance-recipes article{border-top:2px solid var(--color-border);padding-top:16px}
 .appearance-recipes h3{margin-top:0}
 .appearance-recipes dl{display:grid;gap:6px;margin:16px 0 0}
 .appearance-recipes dl div{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-border);padding-bottom:6px}
 .appearance-recipes dt{color:var(--color-muted);font-size:0.85rem}
 .appearance-recipes dd{margin:0;font-size:0.85rem;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;text-align:right}
 .appearance-links{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:16px;margin:28px 0}
 .appearance-links a{display:grid;gap:6px;align-content:start;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:8px;padding:14px;min-height:44px}
 .appearance-links span{font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--color-muted)}
 @media(max-width:800px){.appearance-recipes,.appearance-links{grid-template-columns:1fr}.appearance-contract h2{font-size:1.7rem}}
</style>
